cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this measurement or its figures, please cite it as below."
title: "psrtype-samfyring — ENTSO-E's schema permits two production types per generation unit; no TSO uses it, and three solve multi-fuel plants three different ways"
abstract: >-
  ENTSO-E's GL_MarketDocument schema places TimeSeries at 1..unbounded per
  document, each carrying exactly one psrType, with no uniqueness constraint on
  the generating unit mRID. Two TimeSeries for the same unit with different
  production types are therefore schema-valid. Across 2 191 documents covering
  199 generation units in three bidding zones where biomass co-firing is
  documented in a dated primary source for 2021-2024 -- Finland, Poland and the
  Netherlands -- no unit carries two production types in the same document. Unit
  resolution itself works: Drax appears in GB data with six units under three
  production types simultaneously, so the gap is fuel mixing within a single
  unit. Three TSOs instead use three different single-valued workarounds: PSE
  splits the plant into two production units, TenneT relabels over time, and
  CEPS records a multi-fuel plant as "Other". Neither Regulation (EU) 543/2013
  nor ENTSO-E's Manual of Procedures, to which Article 5(d) delegates the
  classification of production types, contains any of twelve multi-fuel terms.
  Criteria were preregistered and checksummed before the finding was frozen.
  v1.1.0 corrects three claims in v1.0.0 about zone coverage and adds the
  measured downstream effect.
